{"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)","role":"project","title":"Use your first OUDS components","category":"Orange Unified Design System"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"project","sections":[{"kind":"hero","chapter":"Use of first components provided by OUDS","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","title":"Use your first OUDS components","image":"ic_component_intro.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS provides components ready to be used, specified in Figma assets and preventing users to handle tokens.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are rendered thanks to the theme in use.","type":"text"}]}],"backgroundImage":"ic_component_intro.png","estimatedTimeInMinutes":30,"projectFiles":"OUDS-Discovery-Tutorial.zip"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, prepare the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContentView"},{"type":"text","text":" by adding inside it a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","code":"tutorial-discovery-3-1.swift"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-2.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add such picker with three items inside."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-2.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now, let’s add radio buttons to let the user choose its gender."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The official components are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadio"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadioItem"},{"type":"text","text":", but the package has also a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadioPicker"},{"type":"text","text":" to implement quicky a group of radios."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This component can be replaced by your own."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The radio picker is defined by an array of values to display radio items associated to a tag, i.e. an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" thing shared through a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Inside a picker the user can select only one value, not zero."}]}],"type":"step"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-3.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a checkbox item with only two states."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-3.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The radio picker is alone, it is the time to add below a checkbox. OUDS provides two components: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckbox"},{"type":"text","text":" which is a simple checkbox, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckboxItem"},{"type":"text","text":" which is a checkbox (duh!) with additional texts and icons."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The state of the checkbox is shared through a boolean "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In some cases you may need to use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckboxIndeterminate"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckboxItemIndeterminate"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want a three-states checkbox."}]}],"type":"step"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-4.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose to add an instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSHorizontalDivider"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-4.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are also components who do not have any behaviors and are here only for visual rendering, for example dividers which can be horizontal or vertical."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A divider is, in the end, a stroke with a color. You will see later, colors in OUDS have two values: a light mode value, and a dark mode value. Here the divider can have a color which can change, or not."}]}],"type":"step"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-5.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a switch item, it will be used as a trick to force the change of the color scheme for the view for our future operations."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You will then be able to see the automatic changes of colors when you switch the color scheme."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-5.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With radio and checkbox, OUDS provides also switch elements (toggles). They can be alone ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwitch"},{"type":"text","text":") or with texts ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwitchItem"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Just like the checkbox, the switch exposes its state through a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"step"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-6.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSLink"},{"type":"text","text":" in the app and make it open the iOS documentation OUDS website."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-6.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Users may need to navigate outside the app, like, for example, opening a website. Thus the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSLink"},{"type":"text","text":" component can be integrated. It can be only with a text or also a chevron indicator."}]}],"type":"step"},{"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-7.swift","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s add a button with some rules: if checkbox is not checked it is disabled. When tapped, change the style of the button during 5 seconds."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-7.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the end, we can also add a button. Button are one of the most used components in an app and bring a lof of the power and the style of the brand."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can find it with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSButton"},{"type":"text","text":". Such button has an appearance changing its colors, and also a style (loading or not)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thanks to the theme, the enabled, disabled, hover, focus or pressed states are managed."}]}],"type":"step"}],"anchor":"Add-basic-components","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"We will work on a kind of formular using main OUDS components."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Feel free to style and design things as you want."}]}]}],"title":"Add basic components"}]},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"choices":[{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No! The components use the design specifications, i.e. tokens, thanks to the theme, to define the style they must have in all cases."}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}],"isCorrect":false},{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That is the reason why the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSThemeableView"},{"type":"text","text":" is so important: it injects the theme as environment variable so that any component can get it to define its style."}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],"isCorrect":true}],"content":[],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the developer using OUDS component need to manage the look and feel of the components?"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","abstract":[{"text":"Components can be similar to iOS native components, or can also be original and strongly related to Orange Unified Design System needs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"callToAction","title":"Add more OUDS components","action":{"isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"Get started","type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-4-use-other-components"}}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/$volume","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)","modules":[{"projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-librairies#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-librairies#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-librairies"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-librairies"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"